Index the string a string-list property returns, not the property.

GetLocales takes a character of Exts->Strings[Index]. Under clang the
__declspec(property) the transform makes of TStrings::Strings reads a
second subscript as the property's own second index, so the expression is
a two-argument call to the getter and does not compile (parentheses do not
change that). Read into a UnicodeString first, the second subscript indexes
the string the property returns, as under C++Builder. Line counts are
unchanged.

--- a/source/windows/GUIConfiguration.cpp
+++ b/source/windows/GUIConfiguration.cpp
@@ -1246,1 +1246,1 @@
-          AddLocale(AdditionalLanguageMask + Exts->Strings[Index][3], LangName);
+          AddLocale(AdditionalLanguageMask + UnicodeString(Exts->Strings[Index])[3], LangName);
